# The one program (task 30, step 10) runs as the user "one" and never as root.
# It may run exactly one command as the "assistant" user, who owns the
# person's workspace copy and every space: asuser.py, which makes run
# checkouts, lands their work and starts Claude Code with a clean
# environment. Nothing else, and never as root itself.
#
# Every run works as assistant, which may use sudo with nobody asked
# (sudoers-assistant), so a run can do anything on this machine. That is the
# person's decision of 15 September 2026 (D42).
#
# use_pty is off for this user because the command already runs on a
# terminal the program holds; a second terminal inside it would only add a
# layer between the person taking over and the run.
Defaults:one !use_pty, env_reset
one ALL=(assistant) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/python3 -I /srv/one/app/one/asuser.py *
